liblz4 1.9.4, pristine
====================

The pinned oracle installs python-lz4 4.4.4, whose library reports 1.9.4.
The four C/header files here were extracted from the official python-lz4
4.4.4 source distribution's lz4libs/ directory and compared byte for byte
with https://github.com/lz4/lz4/tree/v1.9.4/lib. All four match exactly.
The source distribution omits liblz4's LICENSE; that file was obtained
unchanged from v1.9.4/lib/LICENSE. Its text also matches unityrs-core's
existing LICENSE-LZ4. lz4-1.9.4.sha256 records every file and the official
source distribution's SHA-256. No file in lz4-1.9.4/ has been modified.

build.rs compiles lz4.c and lz4hc.c with renamed exported symbols, hidden
visibility and C heap allocation disabled. Core calls only the HC external
state entry point, at level 9, with fallibly allocated metered state. The
native bridge validates the size and alignment supplied by that caller.
The C/header originals retain their own upstream copyright notices and
are exempt from the repository's Rust/Python source-file size limit.

The LZMA bridge uses the same already-linked static liblzma-sys version as
unityrs-core's decoder. It adds no new third-party package version. The
only build dependency, cc, was already locked by the workspace's codecs.
